From: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: tag_vsc73xx_8021q: use the bridge VID when
 transmitting directly to a bridged port

Joining a bridge replaces a port's standalone tag_8021q VLAN with the
bridge's VLAN (dsa_tag_8021q_bridge_join() adds the bridge VID and
deletes the standalone one). The xmit path, however, only uses the
bridge VID when skb->offload_fwd_mark is set, and otherwise tags with
the standalone VID -- a VID the switch no longer has for that port, so
the frame is dropped.

That is not reachable while everything goes through the bridge, because
bridge-forwarded frames carry the mark. It is reachable as soon as
something transmits straight onto the user port instead: the netfilter
flowtable's direct transmit path does exactly this once
dev_fill_forward_path() has resolved a bridge port, and every packet of
such a flow is then lost.

Measured on an IPQ5332 board with an RTL8372N switch (rtl837x, which
reuses this tagger): with the flowtable forwarding through the bridge,
frames towards the client carry the bridge VID 3088 and arrive; with the
flowtable transmitting directly to the port, they carry the standalone
VID 3076 and the client receives nothing, while the switch's own FDB has
the client on a different port entirely.

So for an unmarked frame to a port of a VLAN-unaware bridge, use the
bridge VID as well and let the switch select the egress port from its own
FDB, exactly as it does for bridge-forwarded traffic.

Everything else is left as it was. Marked frames keep their existing
handling in full: the bridge transmits only one copy per offloaded
hardware domain and relies on the switch to flood it, so they must not be
narrowed to a single port. VLAN-aware bridges are untouched as well --
there every frame carries one of the bridge's own VLANs and tag_8021q
does not decide the egress port.

Link-local traffic (STP, LLDP, EAPOL, PTP peer-delay) is excluded from
the new case, because it is addressed to one specific link and must keep
the precise targeting the standalone VID gives it, the way tag_sja1105.c
tests skb->offload_fwd_mark first and only then carves link-local frames
out of its own imprecise path. For that to work the standalone VLAN has
to stay present in hardware while the port is bridged; the rtl837x driver
keeps it (the port's PVID is the bridge VLAN, so ingress classification
and isolation are unchanged).

Signed-off-by: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/net/dsa/tag_vsc73xx_8021q.c
+++ b/net/dsa/tag_vsc73xx_8021q.c
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 /* Copyright (C) 2024 Pawel Dembicki <paweldembicki@gmail.com>
  */
 #include <linux/dsa/8021q.h>
+#include <linux/etherdevice.h>
 
 #include "tag.h"
 #include "tag_8021q.h"
@@ -13,17 +14,40 @@
 {
 	struct dsa_port *dp = dsa_user_to_port(netdev);
 	u16 queue_mapping = skb_get_queue_mapping(skb);
+	unsigned int bridge_num = dsa_port_bridge_num_get(dp);
+	struct net_device *br = dsa_port_bridge_dev_get(dp);
 	u16 tx_vid = dsa_tag_8021q_standalone_vid(dp);
 	u8 pcp;
 
+	/* A frame the bridge forwarded or flooded is marked, and for an
+	 * offloaded hardware domain the bridge transmits only one copy and
+	 * relies on the switch to flood it. Leave that path exactly as it
+	 * was.
+	 */
 	if (skb->offload_fwd_mark) {
-		unsigned int bridge_num = dsa_port_bridge_num_get(dp);
-		struct net_device *br = dsa_port_bridge_dev_get(dp);
-
 		if (br_vlan_enabled(br))
 			return skb;
 
 		tx_vid = dsa_tag_8021q_bridge_vid(bridge_num);
+	} else if (bridge_num && br && !br_vlan_enabled(br) &&
+		   !is_link_local_ether_addr(eth_hdr(skb)->h_dest)) {
+		/* An unmarked frame bypassed bridge forwarding and was
+		 * transmitted straight onto the user port -- the netfilter
+		 * flowtable's direct transmit path does exactly this. Joining
+		 * a bridge replaced the port's standalone VLAN with the
+		 * bridge's, so tagging with the standalone VID would hand the
+		 * switch a VID it does not have and the frame would be
+		 * dropped. Use the bridge VID and let the switch pick the
+		 * egress port from its own FDB.
+		 *
+		 * Link-local traffic (STP, LLDP, EAPOL, PTP peer-delay) is
+		 * excluded: it is addressed to one specific link and keeps the
+		 * precise targeting the standalone VID gives it, the way
+		 * tag_sja1105.c carves link-local frames out of its own
+		 * imprecise path. The driver keeps that VLAN present in
+		 * hardware while the port is bridged.
+		 */
+		tx_vid = dsa_tag_8021q_bridge_vid(bridge_num);
 	}
 
 	pcp = netdev_txq_to_tc(netdev, queue_mapping);
